#. ja: <sheet Item $n1 0>を読み、<br><sheet ClassJob $n2 0>がレベル<num $n3>になりました！
#. de: Nach der Lektüre <noun-de Item 2 $n1 1 2 1> ist deine Stufe als <sheet ClassJob $n2 0> auf <num $n3> gestiegen!
#. fr: Vous avez lu votre <noun-fr Item 12 $n1 1 1> et avez atteint le niveau <num $n3> pour le job “<sheet ClassJob $n2 0>”.
#. macro: <noun-en Item 3 $n1 1 1> — an English noun from a game data sheet, with article and number; sheet = Item, form = 3, row = number parameter 1, count = 1, case = 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <num $n3> — a number; value = number parameter 3 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <if ($n2 == 10)>an <sheet ClassJob $n2 0><else><if ($n2 == 14)>an <sheet ClassJob $n2 0><else><if ($n2 == 5)>an <sheet ClassJob $n2 0><else><if ($n2 == 26)>an <… — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 2 == 10 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <sheet ClassJob $n2 0> — a value from a game data sheet, such as a name; sheet = ClassJob, row = number parameter 2, column = 0 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
